# License

`lc-base-template` is dual-licensed: **the code is MIT, the learning content is
CC BY 4.0.** Brand assets and the Feijoa typeface are licensed under neither —
see "Brand assets and typeface" below.

Copyright holder for both licenses:
**The Language Centre, University of Cambridge.**

---

## Which license covers what

| Part of the repo                                                    | License                 |
| ------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- |
| `src/`, `scripts/`, build and tooling config, tests                 | MIT                     |
| `lo-config/` — Learning Object manifests, blocks, exercises, modals | CC BY 4.0               |
| `public/audio/`, `public/images/` — authored learning media         | CC BY 4.0               |
| `docs/` — specs, handovers, process notes                           | CC BY 4.0               |
| Cambridge logos, wordmarks and visual-language imagery              | **neither** — see below |
| `public/fonts/feijoa/` (never committed; git-ignored)               | **neither** — see below |

Third-party dependencies are covered by their own licenses. Open Sans, the
public default typeface, is Apache-2.0.

